  "worked_solution": "A logistic growth equation has the form\n\n$$\n{y}^{\u2032}=ky(a-y),\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality, and $a>y$ is the carrying capacity. \n\nThe carrying capacity $a$ represents the maximum possible population. A diagram showing a typical logistic growth curve is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071800/assets/d8133f1c4203903bac606bbae61c73717e2ba2dc15a97a77f48eaaeaf4736d06.png)\n\nFirst, let's rewrite the right-hand side of the given equation so that it matches the form above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{\u2032} & =14.4y-0.003{y}^{2} \\\\  & =0.003y(4800-y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom here, we see that $a=4800.$ Hence, the carrying capacity is $4800,$ and we conclude that the maximum possible population of giraffes is $4800.$",
